  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/0D8X">Exercise <span data-tag="0D8X">111.42.8</span>.</a> Let $A$ be a ring and let $\mathbf{P}^ n_ A = \text{Proj}(A[T_0, \ldots , T_ n])$ be projective space over $A$. Let $F \in A[T_0, \ldots , T_ n]$ be homogeneous of degree $d$. Let $X \subset \mathbf{P}^ n_ A$ be the closed subscheme corresponding to the graded ideal $(F)$ of $A[T_0, \ldots , T_ n]$. What can you say about $H^ i(X, \mathcal{O}_ X)$? </p>
